infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Where you place Suspense is the loading UX
  desc Same data, three boundary placements — three reveals
  lists
    - label One root boundary
      desc All-or-nothing: simplest, but any slow or refetching widget blanks the whole page; first content waits on the slowest query.
    - label A boundary per widget
      desc Independent reveal: fast sections appear at once, slow ones show skeletons — at the cost of popcorn UI and layout shift.
    - label Deliberate grouping (senior default)
      desc Group what users perceive as one unit under one boundary; isolate heavy long-tail sections — coherent yet independent.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b
